# Text files are stored and checked out with LF on every platform, whatever core.autocrlf says (Git for Windows sets it
# to true system-wide, which turned every file CRLF and failed the formatter). Windows-only scripts keep CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
# CHANGELOG.md takes both sides when two landings each add an entry at the top (a union merge), so gate-push's rebase
# never stops on it; the result is still read in review. Nothing else merges this way (scripts/changelog-union.test.ts).
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
